{
  "propositions": [
    "The Pictor Nebula is an emission nebula about 4,000 light-years away that glows due to young stars' radiation and is studied to understand star formation.",
    "The Fornax Loop is a shell of gas shed by an aging star about 9,000 light-years away, studied to trace enrichment of space with heavier elements.",
    "The Fornax Loop is faint and cold, best observed in infrared rather than visible light, and was missed by early surveys until infrared instruments improved.",
    "The Fornax Loop's shell expands outward at about 12 km/s and should disperse within roughly 10,000 years."
  ]
}
